  "releaseNotes": "- fix: a `[<PureView>]` leaf scene-graph view over a real aardvark.dom backend now analyzes (0.1.17 regressed it to a hard error). Three causes, all fixed:\n- **dummy-API namespace shadow**: the reference/test backend's `type Sg` (added for the v2 engine) lived in `namespace Adaptify.PureView`, so a consumer's `open Adaptify.PureView` shadowed `Aardvark.Dom.Sg` — `Sg.Trafo n.Trafo` then saw only the dummy's 2-arg `Trafo(t,c)` (\"a member 'Trafo' taking 1 arguments is not accessible; all accessible versions take 2\"). The dummy type is renamed `DummySg` so it no longer collides. (v1 hid this because the dummy `Sg` didn't exist yet.)\n- **collection-map upcast**: `m.Items |> IndexList.map itemView` yielded into a scene builder (`sg { … }` / a custom `heap { … }`) is wrapped by FCS in a `Coerce` to the builder's `seq<_>` Yield supertype; the analyzer now peels that transparent concrete-collection→seq upcast so the collection-map path fires (the generated alist/aset is what the adaptive builder consumes — the seq supertype is irrelevant).\n- **array-typed adaptive arg**: `Sg.VertexAttribute(\"Positions\", n.Positions)` with `n.Positions : V3f[]` is resolved by FCS to the `(string, System.Array)` overload, wrapping the field in `Coerce(System.Array, …)`. The analyzer now peels that coercion (in the model-dep scan and the emitted args) and recognizes `aval<'a[]>`/`aval<seq>`/`aval<list>`/`aval<option>`/`aval<HashSet>`/`aval<HashMap>` overloads as adaptive consumers, so it emits `Sg.VertexAttribute(\"Positions\", i.Positions)` directly (binding the `aval<'a[]>` overload) instead of an ambiguous `AVal.map`-wrapped form.",
  "title": "Adaptify.PureView",
  "verbatimVersion": "0.1.18",
